dified residue","start":518,"end":518,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Region","start":623,"end":652,"description":"Required for interaction with SRC"},{"type":"Region","start":632,"end":635,"description":"Required for interaction with NEDD4"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":724,"end":724,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":733,"end":876,"description":"EBD domain"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":827,"end":827,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":839,"end":839,"description":"Omega-N-methylarginine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":859,"end":859,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":872,"end":872,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":881,"end":881,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Domain","start":958,"end":996,"description":"UBA"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts with NEDD4 (via WW3 domain). NEDD4L and EGF promote association with NEDD4 (By similarity). Homodimer. Interacts with AR, CDC42, WWASL and WWOX. Interacts with CSPG4 (activated). Interacts with MERTK (activated); stimulates autophosphorylation. May interact (phosphorylated) with HSP90AB1; maintains kinase activity. Interacts with NPHP1. Interacts with SNX9 (via SH3 domain). Interacts with SRC (via SH2 and SH3 domain). Interacts with EGFR, and this interaction is dependent on EGF stimulation and kinase activity of EGFR. Interacts (via kinase domain) with AKT1. Part of a collagen stimulated complex involved in cell migration composed of CDC42, CRK, TNK2 and BCAR1/p130cas. Interacts with BCAR1/p130cas via SH3 domains. Forms complexes with GRB2 and numerous receptor tyrosine kinases (RTK) including LTK, AXL or PDGFRL, in which GRB2 promotes RTK recruitment by TNK2"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q07912-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Miscellaneous","text":"May be produced at very low levels due to a premature stop codon in the mRNA, lea